  <rows>
   <row>
    <id><![CDATA[9002]]></id>
    <qid><![CDATA[1001]]></qid>
    <question><![CDATA[<p>Please give each outcome a score from 1 to 9 for its importance to decisions about therapeutics for filovirus disease:</p><table><tbody><tr><td style="padding:2px 14px 2px 0;"><strong>1–3</strong></td><td>Of limited importance</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 14px 2px 0;"><strong>4–6</strong></td><td>Important</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:2px 14px 2px 0;"><strong>7–9</strong></td><td>Critically important</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The most important outcomes are those that matter to patients – rate these high. If an outcome is “nice to know” or unlikely to change any decision, rate it low. See <a href="https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj-2024-081903" target="_blank">Core GRADE 1: overview of the Core GRADE approach</a> for how these ratings are used.</p>]]></question>
    <help/>
    <script/>
    <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
   </row>
   <row>
    <id><![CDATA[9003]]></id>
    <qid><![CDATA[1002]]></qid>
    <question><![CDATA[How important is each outcome? (1 = of limited importance, 9 = critically important)]]></question>
    <help><![CDATA[Please rate every outcome. If you prefer not to rate one, you can leave it blank and continue.]]></help>
    <script/>
    <language><![CDATA[en]]></language>
